            title: 'Sedma Dominoes',
            subtitle: 'Domino',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Connecting domino game named after the Czech word for seven. Four players receive seven tiles each; no boneyard. Lead rotates; the leader must set a double. Players in turn extend the train from one side only or pass. Points for setting doubles; game to 60.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Sedma (Czech for seven) is a connecting domino game; the layout is built in one direction only and extra points are scored for playing doubles. Related in name to the Czech card game Sedma.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four players use a double-six domino set; each receives seven tiles. There is no boneyard; play is individual with no partnerships.',
